 "decisions": [
  "The route is two snapped tunnels joined by a short daylight clearing: tunnel A (nine straights, four bends) from the west mouth to the exit mouth, a 60 stud clearing, then tunnel B from the east mouth to the east edge. The bible gives only the module mix (18 straights, 8 bends, 3 mouths); the chains were found by a bounded search and fixed as strings (S straight, R bend through end A, L bend through end B).",
  "Joints are computed from the measured end rings (centre and outward facing of ends A and B) with the kit frame (local x = -Blender x); a right bend entered through end B is a left turn, so bends are never mirrored.",
  "Rockfall lanes are 10 studs along the tunnel across the whole 14 stud floor (leaving from the centre takes 0.31 s at 16 studs/s), on the centre of four straight modules, two per tunnel, at least 50 studs apart. The bible does not say which axis the strip is wide on.",
  "Each cave mouth sits on the route with its rear plane on the tunnel joint; the measured gap (+-8.1) contains the 14 stud corridor. The far mouth faces outward, so the exit mouth is turned around.",
  "Nothing stands inside a tunnel: the 14 stud clear width equals the route corridor. Crystal clusters, ore veins, stalagmites and burrows stand on the surface around the approach and the clearing; gather points are measured to those two surface stretches only (8 to 40 studs, facing them).",
  "The route is about 700 studs, far longer than the 19 s sector crossing in the bible, because 26 modules at 24 to 28 studs cannot fit a shorter path. Hostile night rules do not apply here (bible section 2).",
  "Tunnel footprints are convex pieces from the measured geometry: a 25.7 x 24 box per straight and six wedges per bend (radii 5.7 to 31.3 about the arc centre); non-adjacent modules stay at least 2 studs apart."
 ],
